WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.012
- Please welcome Joe Manganiello!

00:00:03.012 --> 00:00:06.619
(audience applauds)

00:00:06.619 --> 00:00:08.640
Hello!
- [Joe] Hi Drew.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.473
Big fan, big fan.

00:00:09.473 --> 00:00:13.250
- Right back at you, for a long time,

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.840
and there's so many things I
wanted to discuss with you.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.770
I guess I could start off

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:23.190
with the beautiful romantic
aspect of your life.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.200
You and Sofia just celebrated

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.478
your fifth wedding anniversary.

00:00:27.478 --> 00:00:30.593
(audience applauds)

00:00:30.593 --> 00:00:31.800
- [Joe] Thank you, yeah.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.500
- That's romantic.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.370
And I was reading about how you said

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.600
that you initially first knew

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.460
that you could really trust each other

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.120
and knew to put each other's priorities

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.450
and that you just kind
of had this, like, system

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.930
of how you started out and
you would stick with it.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:52.473
- I knew because there was
almost like a "Gift of the Magi"

00:00:52.473 --> 00:00:55.260
type of situation,
where unbeknownst to me,

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.590
she had put what I wanted in life

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:00.780
and out of a relationship
or a commitment first

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.810
and unbeknownst to her I had
done the same thing for her,

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.470
so there was this one day in particular

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:07.550
where we both surprised each other

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:11.140
by making some difficult
decisions for each other

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.770
on behalf of the other person,

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:15.480
and in that moment, I knew
that I could trust her.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.170
I knew that she cared about me

00:01:18.268 --> 00:01:21.610
and I cared about her,
obviously, and that was it.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:23.430
And I went ring shopping.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.720
I was actually shooting
"Magic Mike Two" at the time,

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:30.720
so the guys on set were like,
you know, giving me advice,

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.290
you know, about ring shopping
and things like that,

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.520
so it was fun.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.303
Those guys actually had a hand in it,

00:01:38.162 --> 00:01:40.700
in me actually putting the ring on her,

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.950
getting the ring around her finger.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.740
- [Drew] Every woman's fantasy!

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.190
Not only, you know, Joe Manganiello,

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:48.610
but just the cast of
"Magic Mike," you know,

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:49.863
backing it all up.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.520
Jesse Tyler Ferguson
helped set you guys up,

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.600
which is also a total fantasy,

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:59.010
'cause all women hope that someone's going

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.890
to step in and do a setup.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:04.240
There are many movies made
about this whole setup thing

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.930
and it doesn't happen in real life.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.480
- Well, there actually were two friends

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.360
that were instrumental.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:13.710
One was Jesse, yes. Unbeknownst to her.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:18.710
And on my side, I was very
good friends with Jess Cagle,

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.580
who at the time was the editor-in-chief

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.730
of "People Magazine."

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:28.730
Jess actually let me know via
email before anybody else knew

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.780
that she was single so that
I would have the advantage.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:32.940
I needed that advantage

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.300
because she was shooting in New Orleans,

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.480
so I flew straight there.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:41.497
Jess Cagle said, "She's
single, get down there, go."

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.030
- [Drew] And you did.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:49.030
I feel like there might need
to be a movie or a novel

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:54.160
made into; it sounds like
a Hollywood dream fantasy.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.290
And we don't know that it really happens.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:59.750
And to hear that it does is so inspiring

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:03.330
because all women are like,
"If only, like, a guy ever

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:07.220
would, like, book a plane
ticket, show up, anything."

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:11.690
Wow, good for you. And thank
you on behalf of women.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:15.320
- Hey, you know, I guess
I'm old-fashioned and yeah,

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.940
I believe in all of
those stories, you know,

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:20.340
whether it's "Romeo and
Juliet," whatever it is,

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:26.160
you know, I think for
me, my job was to chase

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.470
and I think somebody, whoever
that is, one or the other,

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:32.070
accepts one of the roles and
the other takes the other role,

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:35.170
and you have the opposite
magnets are the ones

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:36.450
that come together, not the same.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.370
So, I mean, we're getting,
like, philosophical here,

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:41.427
but I think that that is the case,

00:03:41.427 --> 00:03:45.260
and I think what gets
confusing is when people

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.630
come at each other with the same polarity,

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:51.760
I think then that can
sometimes deaden out.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:54.180
Somebody has got to chase and
somebody has gotta be chasing.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:55.013
- [Drew] I love it.

00:03:55.013 --> 00:03:57.120
Polarity is one of my very favorite words

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.600
in the English language because it just

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.400
immediately describes
the dynamic of, you know,

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:07.150
it's the perfect antidote
to perfection, I agree.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:09.370
I don't know if you'll
believe this about me, Joe,

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:12.530
but I am a lot of energy,

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.670
so I don't know what my magnet
would be on the other side.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:18.700
There probably some
corpse over in the corner

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.750
who doesn't have much to offer,

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:23.860
that's probably who I
would be magnetized to.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.640
- Well, if you have a lot of energy,

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:28.154
somebody has got to come in with more,

00:04:28.154 --> 00:04:29.380
and that's the thing.
(Drew laughs)

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:32.680
If you want that woman who's
successful and outgoing

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:36.470
and funny and smart, like,
you gotta come in over the top

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.398
and that's, you know, that's a commitment.

00:04:38.398 --> 00:04:41.410
You gotta meet that. You
gotta meet that energy.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:45.160
- I just want to quickly
recommend that you do a Ted talk

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:49.140
on how men should conduct
themselves in the world.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:53.990
I understand that actually, was it Sofia,

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:55.680
do I have this correctly?

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:59.860
That brought a little
someone, if you will,

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.020
into your relationship?

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:06.330
- Yes. So, you know, Sofia wanted a dog.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:10.550
And she, one day, got sent
the picture of this cute,

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:12.483
like the cutest dog you've
ever seen in your life

00:05:12.483 --> 00:05:16.560
in this shelter, "Dogs Without Borders."

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.040
And there was a Saturday morning,

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.180
she said, "Come meet the dog."

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:22.540
And I went, "Oh, I forgot. Okay."

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:26.710
So I walk out and this
cute little thing perks up

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.900
as soon as I walk outside,

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:33.900
jumps off of the lap of
the person from the shelter

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.490
and came running over to me.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:40.830
I said to them, "Okay, you
know, let me, I'll try her out.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:42.950
You can leave her with us for a week."

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.350
So once the shelter people left,

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:50.350
we found out she was sick and
she had a cyst on her belly.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:51.820
- Am I right about this?

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:55.300
Like you knew that something
wasn't right with her

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.360
and you took her to a vet?

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.210
- Yeah, so the next day
I took her to the vet

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.040
and they said, "Well, we're going to try

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.180
to change your diet.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.480
We think there might be
some stones involved.

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:08.060
This cyst might be a cancerous tumor.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:10.250
We don't know, but we're
going to run some tests."

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:13.370
And I said, "I don't
want to run any tests.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.360
Like, here's my credit
card, whatever it costs.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:19.480
You put her into surgery,
you take those stones out.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:20.610
Look at her; she's in pain."

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.840
I kind of felt like the
universe had handed me

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.550
this little thing that needed help.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:28.270
And probably the reason
why she was at the shelter

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:30.330
in the first place, this
cute, sweet little dog,

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:34.290
was because the previous
owners, I'm guessing,

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:37.730
looked at the, you know,
the fees for surgery

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:40.330
and thought, "Well, you
know, we can't do that,"

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.290
and surrendered her.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:45.000
So she was in this spot where
she was going to be put down

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.320
because no families were taking her.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:51.100
She was going to see families
and no one was adopting her.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.870
And so I just thought, you
know what, no matter what,

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:55.950
I'm going to help this little thing out.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:58.290
She's been with us ever
since, she loves me,

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.590
and she's just been like, you know,

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:03.090
the light of our lives
since, since we've had her.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:05.133
- [Drew] Oh my goodness.
- Yeah, there she is.

00:07:05.133 --> 00:07:09.182
- There she is. Oh no, she's so cute.

00:07:09.182 --> 00:07:12.129
Look at that little sausage!
Oh my goodness, okay.

00:07:12.129 --> 00:07:15.296
(upbeat theme music)

